WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.300
Excess share of voice compares your slice of category advertising with your share of market.

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:07.834
Voice minus market is the excess.

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:11.396
Brands that shout louder than their size tend to grow.

00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:16.203
Every ten points of excess is worth roughly half to one point of market share a year.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.260
UNICEF Australia lifted its broadcast share of voice from twenty to fifty-five percent,

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.065
far above its share of donations,

00:00:23.115 --> 00:00:24.810
and awareness rose.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.641
Use it like this:

00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:28.823
compare share of voice with share of market,

00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:30.509
set the gap to fit your growth goal,

00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:32.946
and make the work creative.
